  "id": "architectonic-structure",
  "term": "architectonic structure",
  "definition": "Architectonic structure is the anatomical patterning of the cerebral cortex, especially features such as how clearly its layers are formed. In primates, these structural properties vary along a smooth continuum across cortical areas rather than falling into only completely distinct areas or a fully uniform cortex.",
